Subject: [PATCH] [M157] [scopes] Fix private name resolution in catch scopes and heritage eval

Original change's description:
> [scopes] Fix private name resolution in catch scopes and heritage eval
>
> Fix two issues where private name lookup failed to skip an inner class's
> ClassScope when evaluated inside the class's extends heritage clause:
>
> 1. Delegate the CATCH_SCOPE deserialization constructor in Scope to the
>    standard Scope(zone, CATCH_SCOPE, nullptr, scope_info) constructor so
>    that private_name_lookup_skips_outer_class(), language_mode(),
>    must_use_preparsed_scope_data(), and has_context_cells() are restored
>    from ScopeInfo during lazy compilation. Also mark the enclosing
>    closure scope with RecordNeedsPrivateNameContextChainRecalc() when a
>    non-declaration scope is created in a class heritage position or when
>    RecordEvalCall() is recorded, and clear
>    private_name_lookup_skips_outer_class on inner scopes reparented into
>    an arrow function scope.
>
> 2. Propagate whether a direct eval call is in a class heritage position
>    from BytecodeGenerator::VisitCall to Runtime_ResolvePossiblyDirectEval
>    and Compiler::GetFunctionFromEval. Wrap extends() visitation in
>    BytecodeGenerator::BuildClassLiteral and eval top-level parsing in
>    Parser::ParseProgram with ClassScope::HeritageParsingScope, and
>    restore private_name_lookup_skips_outer_class on synthetic EVAL_SCOPE
>    instances in Scope::DeserializeScopeChain.
>
